> Another aspect of this that I don't understand is that some
> libertarians seem to be opposed to intellectual property, 

Like me.  There is an essential difference between ideas and tangibles.

Tangibles are transferable.  Your gain is my loss or vice versa.  Hence
the concepts of trade, theft and all that.  Ideas, information can be
copied endlessly without loss.  I tell you about my idea.  Now you have
the idea and so do I.  No-one loses.

Some say that someone else's knowledge reduces the income potential of
an idea to, say, the originator.  To which I say, information freely
disseminated is freely accepted.  If an idea has income potential then
it's up to you to keep it a secret from, or form a contract with, the
receiver.

