that they will have to pay for the child's medical care if they decide
to have it.  A society enamoured of genetic determination could ignore
the social reasons -- the poverty, pollution and ignorance -- that can
cause ill health.

	"If we find out that our child has a 50-50 chance of getting a
disease, do we no longer have the option of just accepting the child
